WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
On Wednesday, Russia's

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.269
President, Vladimir Putin, claimed

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:03.937
that Ukraine

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:04.637
was planning

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.706
to use a so-called dirty bomb.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.575
A claim that his underlings

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.377
have been peddling for days.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.379
The accusations were roundly denounced

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.381
by Ukraine and its Western allies.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.983
They say this rhetoric is nothing more

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.785
than a Russian attempt

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.920
to ratchet up tensions and escalate

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.222
the conflict.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.691
So how far will Putin go to turn

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.592
the tide of a war

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.794
that has not gone his way?

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.996
Joining me now is Boris Bonder,

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.665
who spent 20 years as a Russian official.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:33.933
He was a diplomat

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.201
based at the United Nations

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.269
in Geneva before

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.905
resigning in May over the war in Ukraine.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.274
He is one of the highest level officials

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.510
to publicly defect over the war.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.046
And he joins us now from Switzerland.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.913
Welcome, Boris.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:50.150
I want to start by asking you to describe

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.918
why you think

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.287
Russia's decision making and decision

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.321
making apparatus

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.557
got to the point it did

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.459
in the invasion of Ukraine,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.660
because you have this

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.829
fascinating foreign affairs essay

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.965
where you lay out really how Russia

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.900
has evolved

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.169
as a kind of ruling elite in Russia,

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.904
has got narrower,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.306
more and more insulated, more and more

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.610
kind of divorced from the outside world.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.112
What do you think?

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:19.379
You know,

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.313
what happened

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.048
that got us to where we are?

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:25.318
First of all, it did the the result

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:25.952
or outcome

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.388
of this evolution of the Russian state

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.857
which we had

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.859
witnessed for the last 20 years

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.260
and even longer,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.161
it has been

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.029
getting more

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.364
and more isolated from society

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.500
And this is very dangerous

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.935
because people

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.303
who work in the government,

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.405
they get this misinformation

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.107
from their colleagues

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.976
and they make their decision based

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.778
on this miscalculation

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.012
and misinformation.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.814
And we see it as a result of it.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.783
We see it as in the

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.418
the invasion in Ukraine

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.454
in the kind of decision making structure

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.288
you're describing.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.190
Boris, I assume

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.727
bad news does not travel up the chain

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.695
in other words,

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.296
people are not likely to

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.532
to tell Putin, Mr.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.400
President, the war is going badly.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.337
The idea of trying to take Kiev was bad

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.172
all that kind of thing

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.673
probably doesn't go up

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.542
the chain as much as one would hope

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.343
it would.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.179
I believe it is very close to truth

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.848
and I also believe that

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.118
when you report some information

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.721
high to the high command

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:34.988
to you

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.056
and the leadership of the country,

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.392
you have I mean, in Russia today,

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.628
you have to make it

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.830
as pleasant as as possible.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:44.597
And of course,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.299
you don't want to displease

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.201
or upset your bosses

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.702
and the government itself

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.603
because it would

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.238
it would

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.807
jeopardize your career prospects.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:55.875
So

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.279
when we hear this talk about a dirty bomb

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.680
forced by

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.449
Putin's aides, Lavrov now Putin himself,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.952
what do you think is going on inside

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.321
Is is is this.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.291
Are they feeling a certain pressure and

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.128
coming up with new, new threats?

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.730
I think that today

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.401
Russian leadership is actually at a loss.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.637
They're trying to adjust themselves,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.772
accommodate themselves.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.307
To this new reality.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.341
And the reality

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.678
says that Russia may well lose this war.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.546
And, you know, it's

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.582
it looks quite chaotic.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.316
Really,

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.384
because there is no strategy under this.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:42.855
That is only some kind of random ways

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.991
of looking for some opportunities

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.427
to get themselves out of this very,

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:47.927
very,

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.763
very peculiar, very dangerous situation.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:54.601
What about the threat of a nuclear weapon

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.737
being used in your career as a diplomat?

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.938
Have you ever

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.741
heard of the Russian top leadership

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.610
talking about the possible

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.678
use of a tactical nuclear weapon

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.513
Do you think Putin is bluffing

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.915
or is this real?

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.016
I don't think that

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.151
these nuclear nuclear weapons

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.821
threats are very real for now.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:19.425
And I think that they will not be real.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:23.463
If Putin gets the very clear

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.064
signal from international community

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.467
that any use of nuclear weapons

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.902
will have the most grave consequences

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.038
for Russia and for him personally.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.506
And what about negotiations?

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.874
So imagine what you described

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.976
as if Putin feels like he's losing

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.611
and that that fear continues.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.979
That fear continues.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.547
He could end up

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.683
using a tactical nuclear weapon.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:46.352
What if the battlefield ends up

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.220
in a stalemate?

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.756
Let's say the Ukrainians stake

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:50.990
more territory.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.725
Carson, maybe Kharkiv,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.595
but then it bogs down at that point.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.030
Could you imagine

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.399
Putin being willing to arrive

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.166
at some kind

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.868
of negotiated settlement,

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.137
which would be a compromise for everyone?

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.372
All the parties have

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.374
absolutely different and

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.010
antagonizing

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.078
priorities and

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.880
goals in these negotiations.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.681
So for now,

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.449
I don't see any prospects

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.351
for any real negotiation.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.820
So if if what you say is true

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.587
and we are in

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:24.657
for just a long, protracted war,

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.225
what happens inside

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:29.462
Russia is just Putin's hold on Russia

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.732
so strong that even a long war, even

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.167
maybe more mobilization

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.602
would not weaken it at first.

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.672
I don't think that Putin is really ready

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.474
for a long, protracted war.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.609
I think that his strength,

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.545
his regime is a little bit

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.213
overestimated now.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:49.782
And now we see in Russia that

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.451
there is a lot of confusion

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:52.352
in the context

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.087
of mobilization for instance,

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.022
and there is some kind of unrest

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.825
and the discontent within the population.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.561
So I believe that Ukraine may or

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.664
may not go on this

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.966
path of long, protracted war,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.469
but they are capable.

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:12.105
Ukrainian army is capable of defeating

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.106
Russian troops

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:15.608
and of liberating their own flags.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.811
But for that, they need the continued

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.679
and intends

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.880
to seek assistance

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.616
and support from the West But with that,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:27.053
I believe they can win this war

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.488
in quite short terms,

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.223
maybe in a few months.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.458
So because they have already shown

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.228
very significant progress.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:35.995
Boris.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.363
Fascinating insights.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.198
We really appreciate you coming on.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.266
Very, very useful.

